1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:05,320
Meet OpenIDE. Your code, your agent, and your running
app, together in one workspace.

2
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:09,394
Describe the change in the native chat.

3
00:00:10,414 --> 00:00:13,524
Keep your request in view as you explore the project.

4
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:18,973
Project Map reveals connections between files and tests.

5
00:00:19,691 --> 00:00:22,326
Shared memory keeps the conventions that matter.

6
00:00:23,691 --> 00:00:26,778
These tools query the actual project.

7
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:31,658
Review the goal and acceptance criteria before making a
change.

8
00:00:32,337 --> 00:00:36,760
The plan waits for approval, then returns your decision to
the connected client.

9
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:42,056
Inspect the proposed code in the editor's diff view.

10
00:00:44,029 --> 00:00:48,254
Compare the change, save the result, and keep the review
in your workflow.

11
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:54,462
Now check the real app in the integrated browser.

12
00:00:55,995 --> 00:01:00,382
Toggle compact view, filter the list, and verify keyboard
focus.

13
00:01:01,412 --> 00:01:03,512
Your chat draft stays intact.

14
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:06,325
Run the focused tests in the terminal.

15
00:01:07,351 --> 00:01:12,783
This walkthrough also checks the live MCP bridge used by
supported coding clients.

16
00:01:13,351 --> 00:01:15,602
The results come from actual execution.

17
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:19,194
Save a project convention, then read it back.

18
00:01:19,414 --> 00:01:22,826
The next session can start with that shared context.

19
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:26,520
OpenIDE. Explore the source, and make it yours.
